## Remark on the main conjecture `erdos_942`

The main theorem asks whether there exists $c > 0$ such that $h(n) < (\log n)^{c + o(1)}$ eventually and $h(n) > (\log n)^{c - o(1)}$ for infinitely many $n$. This is marked `category research open` and is a genuine open problem. The two results above provide supporting evidence: $\limsup h(n) = \infty$ shows $h(n)$ is unbounded, while the existence of densities shows $h(n)$ has a well-defined distributional structure. However, the precise polylogarithmic bound remains conjectural.

